# FloRun deployment configuration -- copy this file to `config.florun` in the
# WEBROOT (the directory ABOVE the git checkout) and edit.
#
#   cp FloRunWeb/config.florun.example ../config.florun     # from the checkout
#
# config.florun is deliberately NOT in the repo (gitignored) so the nightly
# deploy can never overwrite your edits. It holds NO secrets -- the Cloudflare
# tunnel token lives in a podman secret, never in a file in this directory.
#
# Format: plain KEY=value, no spaces around `=`, no quotes. The updater parses
# this file as DATA (it is never executed), validates every value against the
# character sets noted below, and aborts loudly -- with the running site
# untouched -- on anything suspicious.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# HOSTING THIS YOURSELF (fresh server bootstrap)
#   1. mkdir -p ~/florun && cd ~/florun
#   2. git clone https://github.com/jordanp123/florun.git FloRunWeb
#   3. cp FloRunWeb/config.florun.example config.florun     # edit the values
#   4. Create the tunnel secret (printf, NOT echo -- a trailing newline
#      corrupts the token):
#        printf '%s' 'YOUR-TUNNEL-TOKEN' | podman secret create florun-tunnel-token -
#      Make a tunnel in the Cloudflare Zero Trust dashboard and route your
#      hostname to  http://website:8080
#   5. ./FloRunWeb/deploy/install.sh
#   6. Follow the "Next steps" it prints.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where `git clone` pulls the site from. Used only when the checkout below does
# not exist yet (first run / fresh server); day-to-day the updater runs
# `git pull` inside the existing checkout. Point this at your fork if you have
# one.
REPO_URL=https://github.com/jordanp123/florun.git

# Directory name of the git checkout, created under the webroot. The updater
# passes this to `git clone` explicitly, so it does NOT have to match the repo
# name -- keeping it distinct from the webroot (~/florun/FloRunWeb) is what
# makes "webroot" and "checkout" tellable apart at a glance.
# Letters/digits/._- only.
CHECKOUT_DIR=FloRunWeb

# Unprivileged UIDs the containers run as. Pick a range unused by other stacks
# on the same host -- distinct per-app UIDs mean one compromised container
# cannot touch another app's processes. Both must be BELOW the UserNS size in
# the quadlet units (65536), or the container has nowhere to map and will not
# start; install.sh refuses the install rather than let that fail later.
APP_UID=17011
TUNNEL_UID=17010

# Container-name prefix (must be unique per stack on the host).
# Letters/digits/_- only.
STACK_NAME=FloRun

# URL path segment the site is served under: https://your.domain/<SUBPATH>/
# Letters/digits/._- only. A single dot (SUBPATH=.) serves at the domain root,
# which is the stock FloRun setup -- it expects its own subdomain, e.g.
# florun.example.com, so the service worker controls the whole origin and the
# manifest start_url is simply "/".
#
# If you DO serve from a subpath, point the Cloudflare tunnel route at the
# matching hostname/path; the app itself uses relative URLs throughout and
# needs no other change.
SUBPATH=.
